.TH UPDATESELF 1 "October 2026" "updateself 2.0.0"
.SH NAME
updateself, updsf \- update installed operating-system packages and CLI tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B updateself
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Detects the host and supported installed tools. Runs each updater through its
installation owner. Missing tools are skipped. The default skips confirmations;
use --ask for per-command review. No helpers are installed and no reboot is requested.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print the complete option reference, including component identifiers.
.TP
.B -v, --version
Print the version.
.TP
.B -y, --yes
Skip script and supported package-manager confirmations (default).
.TP
.B -n, --ask
Confirm update commands. Requires a terminal.
.TP
.B -u, --user USER
Choose the non-root account used for user-level tools.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print update commands; allow read-only discovery only.
.TP
.B --only LIST, --skip LIST, --include LIST
Select comma-separated components. Skip takes precedence. Include enables
optional npm, cargo and aur components.
.TP
.B --cleanup, --full-upgrade, --greedy
Opt into backend cleanup, APT dependency-changing upgrades, or additional casks.
.TP
.B --base-install, --apple-install
Install applicable Apple/BSD base updates. Apple may offer major upgrades.
Declarative Nix configuration also requires --nix-config.
.TP
.B --python PATH, --venv PATH, --python-packages
Select interpreters/environments for pip updates. The final flag also updates
their pip-installed packages. Externally managed system Python is respected.
.TP
.B --nix-config KIND, --nix-flake PATH, --nix-update-inputs
Explicit declarative configuration and optional flake input updates.
.TP
.B --log FILE, --no-color, --list-components
Append output to a file, request plain output, or list component identifiers.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
updateself --dry-run
updsf --ask --cleanup
updateself --only snap,flatpak
updateself --only python --venv /home/me/env
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0: completed, skipped or preview; 1: failed update; 2: invalid input/environment;
75: updater lock exists; 130/143: interrupted/terminated.
.SH FILES
Git/archive installations track installed files in PREFIX/share/updateself/manifest.
Per-invoking-user runtime lock: TMPDIR/updateself-UID.lock.
.SH NOTES
Successful commands do not necessarily mean packages changed. Inspect updater
output. --yes cannot bypass authentication or all vendor prompts.
.SH AUTHOR
G. Spanos.
